# Distributions to build the xrdp packages for (./build-xrdp.sh), as
# container images: Debian testing and stable, the latest Ubuntu and its
# two newest LTS, Fedora's next release and the two supported ones.
# Debian 12 is not here: its GNOME (43) lacks libei and Mutter's
# ConnectToEIS (GNOME 46 and newer), which the GNOME backend needs. RHEL 10
# and its rebuilds no longer ship the Xorg server, which xorgxrdp needs.
# Marks after the image (any number, then a note) leave out a feature the
# release cannot give the packages; its Xorg sessions work all the same:
# "no-sway": the release's sway is older than 1.11 (wlroots 0.19), whose
# screen capture protocols (ext-image-copy-capture) the wlroots backend
# needs; xrdp.ini lists no sway session, and the test skips sway.
# "no-kde": the release's plasma-wayland-protocols has no output device
# registry (kde_output_device_registry_v2, 1.21 and newer), which the KWin
# backend needs; it is built without it, and xrdp.ini lists no KDE session.
# "no-av1": the release has no libaom 3.0 or newer (deps/*.txt), which
# xrdp's AV1 encoder needs; it is built without AV1, and clients get H.264
# instead. ./check-deps.sh shows which release needs it.
# "no-av2": built without AV2 (libavm, built from sources.lock, so no release
# needs it today; it is there if one cannot build libavm), and clients get AV1.
debian:testing
debian:13       no-sway no-kde   sway 1.10, plasma-wayland-protocols 1.17
ubuntu:26.10
ubuntu:26.04    no-kde           plasma-wayland-protocols 1.20
ubuntu:24.04    no-sway no-kde   sway 1.9, plasma-wayland-protocols 1.10
fedora:45
fedora:44
fedora:43
